# W62 language injection, the demonstrable partial: a std.fence document with a
# single json fence parses its content with std.json and splices the result under
# an injection node tagged [std.json]. A self-contained proof that injecting one
# embedded language works end to end, independent of the multi-language demo.
<<<cmd
"$TP" run std.fence --input test/suite/inject/inputs/json_only.fence --dump-tree
<<<assert
exit 0
out-contains injection [std.json]
out-contains Object [std.json]
out-contains Array [std.json]
out-contains String [std.json]
out-contains JsonFence
out-absent ERROR
out-absent MISSING
